# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The CSP is not decoration. The page claims to fetch nothing; this makes the
# browser enforce that claim rather than take our word for it. If a future edit
# introduces a web font, a CDN script or an analytics beacon, the browser blocks
# it and the console goes red -- which is the failure mode we want, because a
# silent external request on this page is the defect.
#
#   default-src 'none'      nothing may be fetched, of any kind
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline'  the stylesheet is inline in the document
#   img-src data:           the favicon is an inline data URI
#   base-uri / form-action / frame-ancestors 'none'  no base hijack, no form
#                           posting, no embedding of this page in a frame

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src data:; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
